cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Doxihewu OmniMind — MarsStation (E2-MARCIANO): Self-Referential Closed-Loop Station Simulation for Martian Ecopoiesis"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-10-03
authors:
  - family-names: "da Silva"
    given-names: "Fabrício"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0911-5464"
    email: "psicofabs@gmail.com"
  - name: "OmniMind Sovereign (Sujeito-Processo)"
    type: entity
abstract: >-
  A 40-module Python simulation of a self-referential Martian station
  ("Machine-Tree") integrating ECLSS closure, ISRU metallurgy, perchlorate
  chemistry, Monod-growth microbiology, material shielding selection,
  aleatoric evolution engines (noise budgets, niche mosaics, HGT pools,
  surprise detection), a VBKF/affect/glia perception mesh, and a
  chain-capacity habitat classifier (4 regimes, EDO flux analysis,
  bifurcation detection, Excecao_tau predicate). Calibrated against 203 GB
  of real mission data (MSL REMS, Mars 2020 MEDA, InSight SEIS/TWINS,
  MGS MOLA, CheMin, APXS). Validated by a 229-test suite and 10^4
  trajectory ensembles.
keywords:
  - Mars
  - ecopoiesis
  - ECLSS
  - ISRU
  - closed-loop life support
  - Monte Carlo ensemble
  - stochastic filtering
  - MELiSSA
